          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %em factorization algebra
            is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra+over+an+operad"} algebra over an operad
            where the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/operad"} operad
            in question is like the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/little+disk+operad"} little disk operad
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifold"} manifold
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p
            This way a factorization algebra is an assignment of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+complex"} chain complex
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi V
                    %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V_D
            to each
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ball"} ball
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                  %mo ⊂
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D \subset X
            embedded in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi D
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi D
                    %mi n
                  %mo ⊂
                  %mi D
                  %mo ⊂
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D_1 , \cdots, D_n \subset D \subset X
            sitting inside a bigger embedded ball
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            a morphism
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi V
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi D
                        %mn 1
                  %mo ⊗
                  %msub
                    %mi V
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi D
                        %mn 2
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mo ⊗
                  %msub
                    %mi V
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi D
                        %mi n
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi V
                    %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  V_{D_1} \otimes V_{D_2} \otimes \cdots \otimes V_{D_n} \to V_{D}
          %p such that composition of such operations is suitably respected.
          %p
            In Euclidean (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Wick+rotation"}> Wick rotated
            )
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+theory"} field theory
            factorization algebras serve to axiomatize the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/operator+product+expansion"} operator product expansion
          %h2#definition Definition
          %h3#prefactorization_algebra Prefactorization algebra
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
              write
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Fact
                      %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Fact_X
              be the colored
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/operad"} operad
              in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
              whose
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"}> object
                  s are the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connected"} connected
                  = succeed "s" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+subset"} open subset
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi X
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              %li
                %p
                  the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-set"} hom-set
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Fact
                          %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %msub
                          %mi U
                          %mi i
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                          %mi i
                        %mo ,
                        %mi V
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Fact_X(\{U_i\}_i, V)
                  is the singleton precisely if the
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi U
                          %mi i
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_i
                  are all in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi V
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
                  and are pairwise disjoint and is the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/empty+set"} empty set
                  otherwise.
            %p This specifies composition uniquely.
          #PrefactorizationAlgebra.num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (C, \otimes)
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+category"} symmetric monoidal
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+category"} abelian category
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \in C
              an
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi End
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} End(A)
              be its
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/endomorphism+operad"} endomorphism operad
              %strong prefactorization algebra
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              with values in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra+over+an+operad"} algebra over an operad
              over
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Fact
                      %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Fact_X
              in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℱ
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msub
                      %mi Fact
                      %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi End
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathcal{F} \colon Fact_X \to End(A)
                    \\,.
          %p
            These definitions appear in
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#CostelloGwilliam"} Costello &amp; Gwilliam
          %h3#factorization_algebras Factorization algebras
          #FactorizingCover.num_defn
            %h6#definition_4 Definition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \subset X
              an
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+subset"} open subset
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+cover"} open cover
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi U
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{U_i \hookrightarrow U\}_{i \in I}
              is called a
              %strong factorizing cover
              if for every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+set"} finite set
              of points
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{x_1, \cdots, x_k\} \subset U
              there is a finite subset
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi i
                          %mi j
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi j
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi J
                        %mo ⊂
                        %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{U_{i_j}\}_{j \in J \subset I}
              of pairwise disjoint open subsets such that each point is contained in their union.
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              Every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hausdorff+space"} Hausdorff space
              admits a factorizing cover.
          .num_defn
            %h6#notation Notation
            %p
              For a factorizing cover
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo →
                    %mi U
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{U_i \to U\}_{i \in I}
              write
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P I
              for the set of finite subsets
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi α
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha \subset I
              such that for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi j
                    %mo ,
                    %mi j
                    %mo ′
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi α
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j,j' \in \alpha
              we have
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi j
                      %mo ∩
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mrow
                          %mi j
                          %mo ′
                      %mo =
                      %mi ∅
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_j \cap U_{j'} = \emptyset
            %p
              Given a
              %a{:href => "#PrefactorizationAlgebra"} prefactorization algebra
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℱ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{F}
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi α
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi P
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha \in P I
              write
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℱ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi α
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mrow
                        %mi j
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi α
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathcal{F}(\alpha) := \otimes_{j \in \alpha} F(U_j)
            %p
              and for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi α
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi α
                      %mi k
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi P
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha_1, \cdots, \alpha_k \in P I
              write
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℱ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi α
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi α
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mo ⨂
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi j
                          %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mi ⋯
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi j
                          %mi k
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ∈
                        %msub
                          %mi α
                          %mn 1
                        %mo ×
                        %mi ⋯
                        %mo ×
                        %msub
                          %mi α
                          %mi k
                    %mi ℱ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi j
                          %mn 1
                    %mo ∩
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo ∩
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi j
                          %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathcal{F}(\alpha_1, \cdots, \alpha_k) =
                    \\bigotimes_{(j_1, \cdots, j_k) \in \alpha_1 \times \cdots \times \alpha_k}
                    \\mathcal{F}(U_{j_1} \cap \cdots \cap U_{j_k})
                    \\,.
            %p
              For each
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi i
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1 \leq i \leq k
              there is a canonical morphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mi i
                    %mo :
                    %mi ℱ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi α
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi α
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi ℱ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi α
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi α
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi α
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi α
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    p_i : \mathcal{F}(\alpha_1,\cdots, \alpha_k)
                    \\to
                    \\mathcal{F}(\alpha_1, \cdots, \alpha_{i-1}, \alpha_{i+1}, \cdots, \alpha_k)
                    \\,.
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_5 Definition
            %p
              A prefactorization algebra
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℱ
                    %mo :
                    %msub
                      %mi Fact
                      %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi End
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{F} : Fact_X \to End(C)
              is called a
              %strong factorization algebra
              if for every open subset
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \subset X
              and every
              %a{:href => "#FactorizingCover"} factorizing cover
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo →
                    %mi U
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{U_i \to U\}_{i \in I}
              the sequence
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⨁
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi α
                          %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi α
                          %mn 2
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi P
                        %mi I
                    %mi ℱ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi α
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi α
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi p
                          %mn 1
                        %mo −
                        %msub
                          %mi p
                          %mn 2
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⨁
                      %mrow
                        %mi β
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi P
                        %mi I
                    %mi ℱ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi β
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi ℱ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\bigoplus_{\alpha_1, \alpha_2 \in P I}
                    \\mathcal{F}(\alpha_1, \alpha_2)
                    \\stackrel{p_1 - p_2}{\to}
                    \\bigoplus_{\beta \in P I}
                    \\mathcal{F}(\beta)
                    \\to
                    \\mathcal{F}(U)
                    \\to 0
            %p
              is an
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exact+sequence"} exact sequence
          %p
            These definitions appear
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "http://citeseerx.ist.psu.edu/viewdoc/download?doi=10.1.1.382.8322&rep=rep1&type=pdf"} here
          %p
            See also at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cosheaf"} cosheaf
          %h3#homotopy_factorization_algebras Homotopy factorization algebras
          %p
            Let now
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo ,
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (C,\otimes)
            specifically be a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+chain+complexes"} category of chain complexes
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_6 Definition
            %p
              A [prefactorization algebra]
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℱ
                    %mo :
                    %msub
                      %mi Fact
                      %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi End
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{F} : Fact_X \to End(X)
              is a
              %strong homotopy factorization algebra
              if for all factorizing covers
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo →
                    %mi U
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{U_i \to U \subset X\}_{i \in I}
              the canonical morpshim
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⨁
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                        %mo ≥
                        %mn 0
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⨁
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi α
                          %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mi ⋯
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi α
                          %mi k
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi P
                        %mi I
                    %mi ℱ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi α
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi α
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi k
                    %mo −
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo →
                    %mi ℱ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\bigoplus_{k \geq 0} \bigoplus_{\alpha_1, \cdots, \alpha_k \in P I}
                    \\mathcal{F}(\alpha_1, \cdots, \alpha_k)[k-1]
                    \\to
                    \\mathcal{F}(U)
            %p
              is a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-isomorphism"} quasi-isomorphism
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential"} differential
              on the left is defined by (…).
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_2 Remark
            %p
              This is the analogue of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/descent"} descent
              condition for
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+presheaves"} simplicial presheaves
          %p
            These definitions appear
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "http://citeseerx.ist.psu.edu/viewdoc/download?doi=10.1.1.382.8322&rep=rep1&type=pdf"} here
          %h2#examples Examples
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/beta-gamma+system"} beta-gamma system
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %p Factorization algebras have some similarity with
