          %h2#references References
          %ul
            %li#CostelloGwilliam
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kevin+Costello"}> Kevin Costello
              ,
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Owen+Gwilliam"} Owen Gwilliam
              %em Factorization algebras in quantum field theory
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/CostelloGwilliam-FactorizationAlgebras.pdf", :title => "pdf"}> pdf
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            The notion of factorization algebra may be regarded as a slight variation on the concept
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chiral+algebra"} chiral algebra
            originally introduced in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexander+Beilinson"}> Alexander Beilinson
              ,
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vladimir+Drinfeld"} Vladimir Drinfeld
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chiral+Algebras"} Chiral Algebras
          %p
            A definition formulated genuinely in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higher+Algebra"} Higher Algebra
            appears in section 4.1
            %em Topological Chiral Homology
            of
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacob+Lurie"}> Jacob Lurie
              ,
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/On+the+Classification+of+Topological+Field+Theories"} On the Classification of Topological Field Theories
          %p
            This discusses how locally constant factorization algebras obtained from
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/En-algebras"} En-algebras
            induce
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extended+quantum+field+theory"} extended
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/FQFTs"} FQFTs
          %p
            A fairly comprehensive account of factorization algebras as a formalization of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/perturbation+theory"} perturbative
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+field+theory"} quantum field theory
            (see at
            = succeed ")" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/factorization+algebra+of+observables"} factorization algebra of observables
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kevin+Costello"}> Kevin Costello
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Owen+Gwilliam"} Owen Gwilliam
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Factorization+algebras+in+perturbative+quantum+field+theory"} Factorization algebras in perturbative quantum field theory
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Owen+Gwilliam"}> Owen Gwilliam
                ,
                %em Factorization algebras and free field theories
                PhD thesis (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/GwilliamThesis.pdf", :title => "pdf"}> pdf
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Owen+Gwilliam"}> Owen Gwilliam
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kasia+Rejzner"} Kasia Rejzner
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Comparing nets and factorization algebras of observables: the free scalar field
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1711.06674"} arxiv:1711.06674
          %p and the beginnings of
          %ul
            %li#Costello11
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kevin+Costello"}> Kevin Costello
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Notes on supersymmetric and holomorphic field theories in dimension 2 and 4
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a{:href => "https://www.math.stonybrook.edu/dennisfest/"} Geometric and Algebraic Structures in Mathematics
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1111.4234"} arXiv:1111.4234
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kevin+Costello"}> Kevin Costello
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Claudia+Scheimbauer"} Claudia Scheimbauer
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Lectures on mathematical aspects of (twisted) supersymmetric gauge theories
          %p Lecture notes:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kevin+Costello"} Kevin Costello
                (with
                = succeed ")," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Owen+Gwilliam"} Owen Gwilliam
                %em Factorization algebras in perturbative quantum field theory
                in
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Oberwolfach+Workshop%2C+June+2009+--+Strings%2C+Fields%2C+Topology"} Strings, Field, Topology
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.mfo.de/programme/schedule/2009/24/OWR_2009_28.pdf#page=12"} pdf
              %p
                This can also be found mentioned in the talk notes of the
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Northwestern+TFT+Conference+2009"} Northwestern TFT Conference 2009
              %ul
                %li
                  %p
                    notes by
                    = succeed "," do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Christoph+Wockel"} Christoph Wockel
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/costello.pdf", :title => "Talk by Kevin Costello"} Talk by Kevin Costello
                %li
                  %p
                    notes by Evan Jenkins on the same talk:
                    %a{:href => "http://www.math.uchicago.edu/~ejenkins/notes/nwtft/25may-kc.pdf"} Factorization algebras in perturbative quantum gravity
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Araminta+Amabel"}> Araminta Amabel
                ,
                %em Notes on Factorization Algebras and TQFTs
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2307.01306"}> arXiv:2307.01306
                \&amp;rbrack;
              %blockquote
                %p
                  (with relation to
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functorial+field+theory"} functorial field theory
          %p Further review:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kevin+Costello"}> Kevin Costello
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Owen+Gwilliam"} Owen Gwilliam
              = succeed "," do
                %em Factorization algebra
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Encyclopedia+of+Mathematical+Physics+2nd+ed"} Encyclopedia of Mathematical Physics 2nd ed
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2310.06137"} arXiv:2310.06137
          %p
            There seems to be a close relation between the description of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+field+theory"} quantum field theory
            by factorization algebras and the proposal presented in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stefan+Hollands"}> Stefan Hollands
              , (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0802.2198"}> arXiv:0802.2198
              )
          %p
            The relation of locally constant factorization algebras to higher order
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hochschild+homology"} Hochschild homology
            is in
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gregory+Ginot"}> Gregory Ginot
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thomas+Tradler"} Thomas Tradler
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mahmoud+Zeinalian"} Mahmoud Zeinalian
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Derived higher Hochschild homology, topological chiral homology and factorization algebras
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1011.6483"} arxiv/1011.6483
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gregory+Ginot"}> Gregory Ginot
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Notes on factorization algebras, factorization homology and applications
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1307.5213"} arxiv/1307.5213
          %p A comparison with FQFT for TFTs is presented in
          %ul
            %li
              C. Scheimbauer,
              %em A factorization view on states/observables in topological field theories
              %a{:href => "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=nN-qtnbtpW4"} youtube
              19 min, string-math 2017, Hamburg
          %p
            An
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-category+theory"} (infinity,1)-category theoretic
            treatment of higher factorization algebras is in
          %ul#GaitsgoryFrancis
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dennis+Gaitsgory"}> Dennis Gaitsgory
              ,
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Francis"} John Francis
              %em Chiral Koszul duality
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1103.5803"}> arXiv:1103.5803
              )
          %p
            A construction of
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chiral+differential+operator"} chiral differential operator
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi β
                  %mi γ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta\gamma
            system in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BV+formalism"} BV formalism
            with an intermediate step using factorization algebras:
          %ul
            %li
              Vassily Gorbounov, Owen Gwilliami, Brian Williams,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Chiral differential operators via Batalin-Vilkovisky quantization
              %a{:href => "http://people.mpim-bonn.mpg.de/gwilliam/cdo.pdf"} pdf
            %li
              Brian Williams,
              = succeed "," do
                %em The Virasoro vertex algebra and factorization algebras on Riemann surfaces
              = succeed ":12," do
                %strong 107
              %a{:href => "https://dx.doi.org/10.1007/s11005-017-0982-7"} doi
          %p A version of bosonic string theory related to factorization algebras is presented in
          %ul
            %li
              Owen Gwilliam, Brian Williams,
              %em
                The holomorphic bosonic string?,
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1711.05823"} arxiv/1711.05823
          %p A higher-dimensional generalization of vertex algebras is suggested in the framework of factorization algebras in
          %ul
            %li
              Emily Cliff,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Universal factorization spaces and algebras
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1608.08122"} arxiv/1608.08122
          %blockquote
            %p We introduce categories of weak factorization algebras and factorization spaces, and prove that they are equivalent to the categories of ordinary factorization algebras and spaces, respectively. This allows us to define the pullback of a factorization algebra or space by an 'etale morphism of schemes, and hence to define the notion of a universal factorization space or algebra. This provides a generalization to higher dimensions and to non-linear settings of the notion of a vertex algebra.
          %p
            Relation to
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopical+algebraic+quantum+field+theory"} homotopical algebraic quantum field theory
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Donald+Yau"}> Donald Yau
                ,
                %em Homotopical quantum field theory
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1802.08101"}> arxiv/1802.08101
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Marco+Benini"}> Marco Benini
                , Giorgio Musante,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexander+Schenkel"} Alexander Schenkel
                %em Quantization of Lorentzian free BV theories: factorization algebra vs algebraic quantum field theory
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2212.02546"}> arXiv:2212.02546
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Marco+Benini"}> Marco Benini
                \:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em A stacky approach to the comparison of axiomatizations of quantum field theory
                %a{:href => "CQTS#BeniniNov2024"} talk at
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CQTS"} CQTS
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Benini-CQTS-Nov2024.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Marco+Benini"}> Marco Benini
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Victor+Carmona"} Victor Carmona
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alastair+Grant-Stuart"} Alastair Grant-Stuart
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexander+Schenkel"} Alexander Schenkel
                %em On the equivalence of AQFTs and prefactorization algebras
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2412.07318"}> arXiv:2412.07318
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conformal+net"} Conformal nets
            exhibit factorization algebras
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andre+Henriques"}> Andre Henriques
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Conformal nets are factorization algebras
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1611.05529"} arXiv:1611.05529
          %p
            Relation with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vertex+algebras"} vertex algebras
          %ul
            %li
              Yusuke Nishinaka,
              = succeed "," do
                %em An algebraic construction of functors between vertex algebras and Costello–Gwilliam factorization algebras
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2408.00412"} arXiv:2408.00412
          %blockquote
            %p We construct functors between the category of vertex algebras and that of Costello-Gwilliam factorization algebras on the complex plane ℂ, without analytic structures such as differentiable vector spaces, nuclear spaces, and bornological vector spaces. We prove that this pair of functors is an adjoint pair and that the functor from vertex algebras to factorization algebras is fully faithful. Also, we identify the class of factorization algebras that are categorically equivalent to vertex algebras. To illustrate, we check the compatibility with the commutative structures and the factorization algebras constructed as factorization envelopes, including the Kac-Moody factorization algebra, the quantum observables of the βγ system, and the Virasoro factorization algebra.
          %p A very general treatment of factorization algebras is given in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Clark+Barwick"}> Clark Barwick
              ,
              %em Factorization algebras in quite a lot of generality
              (2025) &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://webhomes.maths.ed.ac.uk/~cbarwick/papers/facts.pdf"}> pdf
              \&amp;rbrack;
        .revisedby
